<meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=UTF-8"/><html> <head><title><h1>Report</h1></title></head> <br> <body BGCOLOR =#ffffff><table  border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;font-size: 14px;" align="center" width="100%" padding-top="100px"  cellspacing="0" cellpadding="5" bordercolor="#ccc"> <tr> <td width="50%" border=0><b>Name&nbsp;:</b>&nbsp;SHANTI DEVI   </td> <td width="50%"><b>Pat ID&nbsp;:</b>&nbsp;E:04/09/2017 13:35:57</td> </tr> <tr><td width="50%"><b>Age&nbsp;:</b>&nbsp;062Y</td><td width="50%"><b>Sex&nbsp;:</b>&nbsp;F</td></tr> <tr> <td width="50%"><b>DOB&nbsp;:</b>&nbsp;00/00/0000</td><td width="50%"><b>Modality&nbsp;:</b>&nbsp;MR</td></tr> <tr><td width="50%"><b>Date&nbsp;:</b>&nbsp; 09/04/2017</td> <td width="50%"><b>Time&nbsp;:</b>&nbsp; 16:51:01</td> </tr> <tr> <td width="50%"><b>Radiologist&nbsp;:</b>&nbsp;Dr.Desai</td> <td width="50%"><b>Ref. Doctor&nbsp;:</b>&nbsp;DR.A.K.SINGH MCH NEURO    </td></tr> </tr></tr></table><br> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>MR BRAIN:</strong></span></p>
<p><strong><span>&nbsp;</span></strong></p>
<p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><span>Protocol:</span></span></strong><span>Brain was studied in axial, coronal and sagittal planes with 5mm slices thickness. T1 and T2WI images were obtained.</span></p>
<p><span>&nbsp;</span></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Observations:</span></strong></p>
<p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">There is evidence of a gliotic infarct in the right occipital cortical and subcortical region with ex vacuo dilatation of the occipital horn of the right lateral ventricle.</span></strong></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>There is no shift of the midline structures.&nbsp;</p>
<p><span>&nbsp;</span></p>
<p><span>Cortical gray matter and underlying white matter reveal normal signal intensity pattern.&nbsp; </span></p>
<p><span>&nbsp;</span></p>
<p><span>Posterior fossa structures appear normal.</span></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>The rest of the ventricular system is unremarkable.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong><span>&nbsp;</span></strong></p>
<p><strong><span>&nbsp;</span></strong><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Conclusion:</span></strong></p>
<p><strong>This examination reveals&nbsp;<strong><span>a gliotic infarct in the right occipital cortical and subcortical region with ex vacuo dilatation of the occipital horn of the right lateral ventricle.</span></strong></strong></p><br><img src=http://139.162.8.237/medpac/analizer/signatures/dr.desai.jpg /><br>  Dr.Desai <br> DNB <br> Consultant Radiologist</body></html><BR><BR><div style="font-size:x-small">Investigations have their limitations. Solitary pathologic al/Radiological and other investigations never confirm the final diagnosis. They only
help in diagnosing the disease in correlation to clinical symptoms and other related tests. Please interpret accordingly.<BR><BR>This Report is not for Medico - Legal Purposes</div></body>
